WEBVTT

00:00.931 --> 00:04.110
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.210 --> 00:07.479
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.513 --> 00:11.049
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.083 --> 00:14.052
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.086 --> 00:17.555
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.821 --> 00:21.124
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.158 --> 00:22.692
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.726 --> 00:24.026
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.061 --> 00:25.668
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.671 --> 00:37.006
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Muppet Babies.</i>

00:37.040 --> 00:40.309
Piggy, I don't think
Kermie Jr. is doing so well.

00:40.344 --> 00:44.147
Kill me!
I'm in constant pain!

00:44.181 --> 00:45.381
(knocking)

00:46.416 --> 00:47.583
hey, Quagmire.

00:47.618 --> 00:50.353
Hey, Peter, do you mind
if I hang out here a while?

00:50.387 --> 00:51.687
I accidentally made
eye contact

00:51.722 --> 00:54.557
with a transvestite at a bar,
and he followed me home.

00:54.591 --> 00:56.159
You knew what you
were staring at!

00:56.193 --> 00:58.461
Get out of here, you mess!
You were far away!

00:58.495 --> 00:59.729
I didn't know
what you were!

00:59.763 --> 01:01.831
You know you want me!
Shut up! Now go home!

01:01.865 --> 01:02.999
Nobody saw me come here!

01:03.033 --> 01:04.000
I said, shut up!

01:04.034 --> 01:05.194
(whispers):
Sneak around back.

01:05.202 --> 01:06.469
Oh, sure.
Come on in, Quagmire.

01:06.503 --> 01:08.304
Oh, you don't have
to take your shoes off.

01:08.338 --> 01:09.739
Our house sucks.

01:09.773 --> 01:11.908
So, Quagmire, if you're
some kind of big ladies' man,

01:11.942 --> 01:14.010
how come I never see you
wearing a necklace?

01:14.044 --> 01:15.945
I, uh... that's
not really my thing.

01:15.979 --> 01:17.213
I'll get you one.

01:17.247 --> 01:18.881
Please don't.

01:18.916 --> 01:20.049
(a la Vinny):
Hey, come on!

01:20.083 --> 01:21.617
The guy wants
to get you a necklace,

01:21.652 --> 01:22.885
let him get you a necklace!

01:25.923 --> 01:29.358
(insect buzzing)

01:29.393 --> 01:31.294
Ah! Ah!
There's a bee in here!

01:31.328 --> 01:32.395
(screams)

01:32.429 --> 01:34.397
(both scream)

01:34.431 --> 01:35.832
(harmonized screaming)

01:35.866 --> 01:37.800
Can you take it up here...?

01:41.004 --> 01:43.072
Wow, we sound
amazing together!

01:43.106 --> 01:44.607
I know!
That was incredible!

01:44.641 --> 01:46.576
You know, we should do
something with this.

01:46.610 --> 01:48.644
Yeah, maybe we could open up
a mattress store.

01:48.679 --> 01:49.979
Or we could try singing.

01:50.013 --> 01:50.980
Yeah, singing,
that's good!

01:51.014 --> 01:52.515
Wow, finally,
something in my life

01:52.549 --> 01:53.916
that makes me feel special.

01:53.951 --> 01:56.252
I mean, except for when
I had those cow udders.

01:56.286 --> 01:58.120
So, as you can see,
the fiscal projections

01:58.155 --> 02:00.523
for the fourth quarter make
this thing a slam dunk.

02:00.557 --> 02:02.158
Any questions?

02:02.192 --> 02:03.960
Not about my cow udders.

02:03.994 --> 02:06.162
All right, then, looks like
we got ourselves a deal.

02:06.196 --> 02:08.331
This is cause
for celebration.

02:08.365 --> 02:09.398
(cork popping sound)

02:09.433 --> 02:11.834
(all cheering)

02:11.869 --> 02:14.804
(chuckles) I don't care,
I'm not driving.

02:19.343 --> 02:21.310
Okay, what do you got
for a lyric?

02:21.345 --> 02:23.613
"I put a booger on a
painting at the museum."

02:23.647 --> 02:24.914
Is that... is
that anything?

02:24.948 --> 02:25.982
Maybe, maybe.

02:26.016 --> 02:28.150
All right, I got one.

02:28.185 --> 02:31.654
♪ Alyssa Milano

02:31.688 --> 02:34.257
♪ I knew you were gonna be hot

02:34.291 --> 02:35.892
♪ When you were nine.

02:35.926 --> 02:37.426
How about this?

02:37.461 --> 02:41.797
♪ Every food tastes good
with melted cheese ♪

02:41.832 --> 02:45.134
♪ I like twins,
unless they're Siamese. ♪

02:45.168 --> 02:48.037
There you go!
Now we're jazzin'.

02:49.907 --> 02:54.343
♪ Don't store your condoms
in your billfold ♪

02:54.378 --> 02:58.014
♪ Those things don't work
if they get dry and old ♪

02:58.048 --> 03:00.883
♪ Broken rubber...

03:00.918 --> 03:04.553
♪ Broken rubber!

03:04.588 --> 03:06.889
CHRIS: Guys, I'm trying to do
something up here

03:06.924 --> 03:09.725
that works better
if I don't hear men singing!

03:09.760 --> 03:11.494
Oh, damn,
we're out of paper.

03:11.528 --> 03:13.229
Oh, we'll get some more
down at Mort's.

03:13.263 --> 03:14.931
But, Quagmire,
we are on fire here!

03:14.965 --> 03:17.166
We're gonna be the best thing
since sliced bread!

03:17.200 --> 03:19.635
I'd like a sandwich,
but I don't feel like eating

03:19.670 --> 03:21.904
two whole loaves of bread.

03:21.939 --> 03:23.506
Tough (bleep)!

03:26.576 --> 03:28.044
Hey, do you mind
paying for this?

03:28.078 --> 03:29.211
I don't have any cash.

03:29.246 --> 03:31.047
Sure, I'll just put it
on my credit card.

03:31.081 --> 03:32.682
I'm never gonna
pay it back anyway.

03:32.716 --> 03:36.385
♪ 'Cause I have $30,000
in credit card debt ♪

03:36.420 --> 03:39.121
♪ When they call,
I tell them ♪

03:39.156 --> 03:40.823
♪ I can't pay it back yet

03:40.857 --> 03:41.891
♪ Credit card debt

03:41.925 --> 03:43.726
♪ Tomorrow I may buy myself

03:43.760 --> 03:45.194
♪ A dining room set

03:45.228 --> 03:46.629
Or this Boba Fett!

03:46.663 --> 03:48.764
♪ Credit card debt,
credit card debt ♪

03:48.799 --> 03:49.899
♪ Credit card debt.

03:49.933 --> 03:51.367
What is that sound?

03:51.401 --> 03:54.270
It's like two Mandy Patinkins
walked into my store!

03:54.304 --> 03:55.571
Was that you guys singing?

03:55.605 --> 03:56.639
Yeah.

03:56.673 --> 03:58.941
That was beautiful.
And it must be original,

03:58.976 --> 04:00.843
because I know every song
about money,

04:00.877 --> 04:02.712
and I've never heard
that one before.

04:02.746 --> 04:04.947
Well, it was based
on actual events.

04:04.982 --> 04:07.149
Although, I-I don't have
as cavalier an attitude

04:07.184 --> 04:09.618
toward my debt
as the song suggests.

04:09.653 --> 04:11.053
I'm-I'm actually
up most nights

04:11.088 --> 04:12.688
with severe
panic attacks.

04:12.723 --> 04:14.690
I-I've taken to
throwing up in the yard

04:14.725 --> 04:16.225
so my wife
won't hear me.

04:16.259 --> 04:17.760
Well, you guys have got
something special

04:17.794 --> 04:19.028
with those harmonies.

04:19.062 --> 04:20.930
They could give me five
years salary, tax free,

04:20.964 --> 04:22.999
and it wouldn't put
a dent in my problem.

04:23.033 --> 04:24.200
You really think
we're good?

04:24.234 --> 04:25.201
Oh, yeah.

04:25.235 --> 04:26.235
And I should know.

04:26.269 --> 04:27.670
Back in the 1970s,

04:27.704 --> 04:30.840
I used to have my own
record label, Mort Town.

04:30.874 --> 04:34.710
<i>I managed
all the hottest disco acts.</i>

04:34.745 --> 04:36.979
<i>I even managed
Earth, Wind, Fire & Pollen</i>

04:37.014 --> 04:39.548
<i>for a little while,
but I had to give it up.</i>

04:39.583 --> 04:40.816
♪ Do you remember

04:40.851 --> 04:41.817
(Mort sneezes)

04:41.852 --> 04:44.887
♪ The 21st night
of September? ♪

04:44.921 --> 04:46.255
(Mort sneezes)

04:46.289 --> 04:49.458
Oh! September is
the worst month for pollen!

04:49.493 --> 04:50.726
<i>I had it all.</i>

04:50.761 --> 04:53.195
<i>But it soon all came
to a very ugly end.</i>

04:53.230 --> 04:54.630
<i>QUAGMIRE:
How come?</i>

04:54.664 --> 04:57.433
<i>MORT: I got addicted to olives.
They were everywhere.</i>

04:57.467 --> 05:00.036
<i>It was so easy to get
your hands on them.</i>

05:03.640 --> 05:04.874
<i>It was awful.</i>

05:04.908 --> 05:06.142
<i>I lost weight,</i>

05:06.176 --> 05:09.045
<i>my hair straightened,
even my voice changed.</i>

05:09.079 --> 05:12.214
<i>I didn't recognize the man
I saw in the mirror.</i>

05:12.249 --> 05:14.884
(deep voice): What has happened
to you, Mort Goldman?

05:14.918 --> 05:17.053
You've hit rock bottom.

05:17.087 --> 05:19.422
I'm lucky to be alive today.

05:19.456 --> 05:21.157
Anyway, you guys got the talent,

05:21.191 --> 05:22.725
but what you need
is a manager.

05:22.759 --> 05:24.026
Someone with no talent

05:24.061 --> 05:26.062
who can take a lion's share
of your earnings.

05:26.096 --> 05:27.396
You'd do that for us?

05:27.431 --> 05:29.231
Sure I would.
So, what do you say?

05:29.266 --> 05:30.866
Can I be your manager?

05:30.901 --> 05:32.168
You betcha!
All right!

05:32.202 --> 05:33.169
Put her there!

05:33.203 --> 05:34.870
No, I've seen
your prescriptions.

05:34.905 --> 05:36.505
Let's just say
we're doing it.

05:36.540 --> 05:38.240
Well, Mort, I hope
I can trust you.

05:38.275 --> 05:39.508
I've been lied to before.

05:39.543 --> 05:41.377
Well, I'm off to work.
Bye, guys! Love you!

05:41.411 --> 05:42.378
Love you, too!

05:42.412 --> 05:43.612
Bye! Love you!
Love you, Pop!

05:43.647 --> 05:44.814
(all laugh)

05:44.848 --> 05:46.115
CHRIS:
He bought it!

05:46.149 --> 05:47.183
STEWIE:
What an idiot!

05:47.217 --> 05:49.051
LOIS: I hate him so much
I'm shaking!

05:52.089 --> 05:53.489
(guitars tuning)

05:53.523 --> 05:56.125
All right, fellas,
open mic at the library.

05:56.159 --> 05:57.860
Your first gig.
Go get 'em!

05:57.894 --> 06:00.696
Hey, do I have time to get
a drink at the water fountain

06:00.730 --> 06:02.765
where the water does not crest
above the dispenser?

06:02.799 --> 06:03.799
Sure.

06:06.336 --> 06:07.970
(slurping)

06:10.107 --> 06:12.842
I can taste
the previous person's cough.

06:12.876 --> 06:14.243
Fellow cardholders,

06:14.277 --> 06:18.047
please put your hands together
for Griffin and Quagmire!

06:18.081 --> 06:19.381
(soft ballad playing)

06:22.152 --> 06:25.154
♪ I can't poop
in strange places ♪

06:25.188 --> 06:26.722
♪ Strange places

06:26.756 --> 06:30.659
♪ I can only poop
in my home ♪

06:30.694 --> 06:34.063
♪ It's as though
I'm watched by strange faces ♪

06:34.097 --> 06:35.831
♪ Strange faces

06:35.866 --> 06:40.202
♪ It's why I never roam

06:40.237 --> 06:41.537
Excuse me,
I just want

06:41.571 --> 06:43.472
to grab one of
those newspapers.

06:45.876 --> 06:47.643
Just grab one
and go!

06:47.677 --> 06:50.146
I'm looking for a job, okay?!

06:52.716 --> 06:56.585
♪ I've left Stewie alone
with strangers ♪

06:56.620 --> 06:58.020
♪ Strangers

06:58.054 --> 07:02.391
♪ To satisfy
my fecal needs ♪

07:02.425 --> 07:07.129
♪ I've put my whole family
in danger ♪

07:07.164 --> 07:11.867
♪ To poop
before my anus bleeds ♪

07:11.902 --> 07:16.906
♪ Home bowl, home bowl

07:16.940 --> 07:21.477
♪ You know just what I need

07:21.511 --> 07:25.848
♪ Home bowl, home bowl

07:25.882 --> 07:29.785
♪ Poop before my anus bleeds.

07:31.588 --> 07:33.622
Aw, everybody left.

07:33.657 --> 07:35.057
Well, this was
a waste of time.

07:35.091 --> 07:37.259
I could have gone hiking
with the girls.

07:37.294 --> 07:38.427
We don't hike.

07:38.461 --> 07:40.930
We just wear tight pants
and get coffee.

07:44.100 --> 07:46.502
Well, I guess no one cares
about our music.

07:46.536 --> 07:48.237
I thought we were
pretty good.

07:48.271 --> 07:50.272
Yeah, I've seen
worse performances.

07:50.307 --> 07:53.776
I was walking home around
8:15 p.m. to my car.

07:53.810 --> 07:56.545
It was very dark, and then
I-I heard the footsteps...

07:56.580 --> 07:59.248
Boo! Get to the sex!

07:59.282 --> 08:00.950
Guys, I got great news!

08:00.984 --> 08:02.418
Oh, what is it, Mort?

08:02.452 --> 08:04.620
I put your performance
on JewTube.

08:04.654 --> 08:07.122
The promoters of the New England
Music Festival saw it,

08:07.157 --> 08:08.624
and they want
to book you!

08:08.658 --> 08:10.059
What?!
Are you kidding me?!

08:10.093 --> 08:11.727
Oh, my God,
you hear that, Quagmire?

08:11.761 --> 08:12.995
We're on our way!

08:13.029 --> 08:15.864
We got to celebrate like
girls in their 20s!

08:15.899 --> 08:18.033
(camera clicking, all giggling)

08:22.405 --> 08:25.474
PETER:
Oh, my God, we are so random!

08:29.781 --> 08:32.483
You got booked at
the New England Music Festival?

08:32.517 --> 08:34.418
Oh, my God, Peter,
that's amazing!

08:34.453 --> 08:37.288
I had no idea you and Quagmire
could even sing!

08:37.322 --> 08:39.457
Now let this be
a lesson to you kids.

08:39.491 --> 08:41.592
If you randomly stumble
upon an amazing talent,

08:41.627 --> 08:44.262
and then someone important
sees it by wild coincidence,

08:44.296 --> 08:46.530
great things can happen
without any hard work.

08:46.565 --> 08:49.500
I'm gonna go jump off
the roof and see if I can fly!

08:49.534 --> 08:51.636
That's it, Chris,
pursue your dream!

08:51.670 --> 08:53.971
A singer, huh?
You as good as the guys

08:54.006 --> 08:56.073
who sing "Happy Birthday"
at Macaroni Grill?

08:56.108 --> 08:57.208
Oh, don't compare me...

08:57.242 --> 08:58.603
Look, they been doing it
for years.

08:58.610 --> 09:01.279
Imagine, my Peter,
the big singing star!

09:01.313 --> 09:04.382
Don't forget about us squares
back at home.

09:04.416 --> 09:05.583
Don't you worry, Lois.

09:05.617 --> 09:07.084
No one has stronger marriages

09:07.119 --> 09:09.854
and more well-adjusted kids
an rock stars.

09:09.888 --> 09:11.422
It's working!

09:17.462 --> 09:19.196
What you doing
with that doll?

09:19.231 --> 09:20.498
Oh, hello, Vinny.

09:20.532 --> 09:22.900
Rupert and I are just having
a spritzer and some cheese

09:22.934 --> 09:24.302
in advance
of the performance.

09:24.336 --> 09:25.903
I wouldn't do that.
Why not?

09:25.937 --> 09:27.338
You know,
there was a guy

09:27.372 --> 09:28.773
on my old block,
Johnny Chickstuff.

09:28.807 --> 09:31.175
We called him that because
he used to like to, uh...

09:31.209 --> 09:32.276
Do chick stuff?

09:32.311 --> 09:33.577
Do chick stuff!
Exactly.

09:33.612 --> 09:35.212
Anyway, a bunch of us
got together

09:35.247 --> 09:38.482
and beat him with a grill lid
and windshield wipers,

09:38.517 --> 09:41.252
and let's just say, uh, he
don't do chick stuff no more.

09:41.286 --> 09:42.586
'Cause of the beatin's?

09:42.621 --> 09:44.522
Yeah. He wasn't
exactly like us,

09:44.556 --> 09:46.290
so we had to
almost kill him.

09:46.325 --> 09:48.392
That sounds terrible.
What happened to him?

09:48.427 --> 09:49.760
I don't know.
Soon thereafter,

09:49.795 --> 09:51.996
a girl in the neighborhood
married a black guy,

09:52.030 --> 09:54.699
so we all kind of turned
our attention to that.

09:54.733 --> 09:56.901
(guitars tuning)

09:56.935 --> 09:58.235
Look at us, Quagmire.

09:58.270 --> 10:00.071
We're making music,
living the dream.

10:00.105 --> 10:01.839
And to think,
just last week,

10:01.873 --> 10:04.775
my only creative outlet was
picking hockey fights at work.

10:04.810 --> 10:07.011
Griffin, I need
these shipping reports

10:07.045 --> 10:08.879
filled out by 5:00 today.

10:14.953 --> 10:17.321
Hey, Peter, I just wanted
to wish you good luck.

10:17.356 --> 10:18.756
Oh, that's great.
Thank you so much.

10:18.790 --> 10:19.757
What's your name, honey?

10:19.791 --> 10:20.958
It's me, Lois.

10:20.992 --> 10:22.059
All right,
backstage whore,

10:22.094 --> 10:23.561
here's the key
to my hotel room.

10:23.595 --> 10:25.575
You can flush the dump
I left in there.

10:25.576 --> 10:26.093
What?!

10:26.098 --> 10:27.398
ANNOUNCER:
Ladies and gentlemen,

10:27.432 --> 10:29.734
please welcome
Griffin and Quagmire!

10:29.768 --> 10:30.901
Peter, we're on!

10:31.903 --> 10:33.637
(crowd cheering)

10:33.672 --> 10:35.673
(playing folk music)

10:37.509 --> 10:39.944
♪ Have you ever put butter
on a Pop-Tart? ♪

10:39.978 --> 10:42.480
♪ It's so frickin' good

10:42.514 --> 10:44.615
♪ Have you ever put butter
on a Pop-Tart? ♪

10:44.649 --> 10:47.651
♪ If you haven't,
then I think you should ♪

10:47.686 --> 10:49.520
♪ I was sittin' in the kitchen
one day ♪

10:49.554 --> 10:51.088
♪ And I was itchin'
to fill up my belly ♪

10:51.123 --> 10:52.423
♪ With the pipin' hot jelly

10:52.457 --> 10:54.091
♪ Of the best damn treat
in the world ♪

10:54.126 --> 10:55.593
He's talking Pop-Tarts!

10:55.627 --> 10:58.295
♪ And I saw a stick of butter
and it almost made me shudder ♪

10:58.330 --> 11:01.332
♪ And scream like a baby girl

11:01.366 --> 11:03.401
♪ I don't want a giant penis
or a rocket trip to Venus ♪

11:03.435 --> 11:05.569
♪ I don't want
to win the lottery ♪

11:05.604 --> 11:06.704
♪ I just want to squat
and gobble ♪

11:06.738 --> 11:08.072
♪ Till I'm dizzy and I wobble

11:08.106 --> 11:09.740
♪ In a butter, fruit
and dough tart dream ♪

11:09.775 --> 11:12.076
♪ So I put butter
on a Pop-Tart ♪

11:12.110 --> 11:14.578
♪ It was so frickin' good

11:14.613 --> 11:16.847
♪ Have you ever put
butter on a Pop-Tart? ♪

11:16.882 --> 11:19.583
♪ If you haven't,
then I think you should ♪

11:19.618 --> 11:21.419
Everybody come
along with us!

11:21.453 --> 11:23.888
♪ Have you ever put butter on a... ♪
CROWD: Pop-Tart!

11:23.922 --> 11:25.756
♪ It's so frickin' good
Yeah!

11:25.791 --> 11:27.691
♪ Have you ever put
butter on a... ♪

11:27.726 --> 11:29.326
CROWD: Pop-Tart!
♪ If you haven't

11:29.361 --> 11:31.061
♪ Then I think you should.

11:31.096 --> 11:32.096
Pop-Tart!

11:32.130 --> 11:34.298
With butter?!

11:34.332 --> 11:36.333
(crowd cheering)

11:39.704 --> 11:41.138
Hey, you guys were great.

11:41.173 --> 11:42.573
Aw, thanks.
My name's Ricky.

11:42.607 --> 11:43.974
I'm with Sony Records.

11:44.009 --> 11:46.210
Our company's gonna be around
for at least three more weeks,

11:46.244 --> 11:48.145
and we want to sign you.

11:48.180 --> 11:50.648
I'll need to discuss this
with my associate.

11:50.682 --> 11:53.050
I don't know, it-it seems
wrong to just dump Mort.

11:53.084 --> 11:54.718
He's our friend.
Doesn't that matter?

11:54.753 --> 11:57.054
Quagmire, you remember I told
you about that dream I drew?

11:57.088 --> 11:59.089
Yeah?
We're halfway there.

11:59.124 --> 12:01.292
I think if we do this,
we'll get the giraffe.

12:01.326 --> 12:02.793
Okay, okay, I'm in.

12:02.828 --> 12:03.894
You got a deal.

12:03.929 --> 12:05.596
Great!
I'm gonna get you on tour.

12:05.630 --> 12:08.499
This is the beginning
of something big.

12:08.533 --> 12:09.867
Great news, guys!

12:09.901 --> 12:12.503
I may have gotten you booked
at a horse's birthday party.

12:12.537 --> 12:14.104
Mort, you're fired.
What?

12:14.139 --> 12:16.140
Sorry, Mort, but this is
a cutthroat business.

12:16.174 --> 12:18.108
And we need someone tough
in our corner.

12:18.143 --> 12:21.145
Like Indonesian kickboxer
Agoos Bahnwati.

12:21.179 --> 12:23.314
Come on. Come on.

12:23.348 --> 12:24.949
Come on,
come on.

12:24.983 --> 12:26.717
Disappear, disappear.

12:26.751 --> 12:28.953
Come on. Come on.

12:33.492 --> 12:35.259
Peter, I heard you fired Mort.

12:35.293 --> 12:36.594
He's your friend.

12:36.628 --> 12:38.796
He's the one that got you
to where you are today.

12:38.830 --> 12:41.565
Lois, my transcendent talent
got me to where I am.

12:41.600 --> 12:44.168
Peter, I don't like what
success is doing to you.

12:44.202 --> 12:46.337
Yeah, well, I don't like
what time is doing to you.

12:46.371 --> 12:48.572
Droop, droop...
(imitates explosion)

12:48.607 --> 12:50.241
Hey, Chris, you ready
with my luggage?

12:50.275 --> 12:51.542
Luggage? For what?

12:51.576 --> 12:53.177
We're going on tour, Lois.

12:53.211 --> 12:54.445
Here you go, Dad.

12:54.479 --> 12:56.680
I emptied this out so
it'd be easier to carry.

12:56.715 --> 12:58.282
Oh, you're right, it is easier.

12:58.316 --> 12:59.316
Good thinking, son.

12:59.351 --> 13:00.918
All right, see you guys
in two months.

13:00.952 --> 13:02.686
Peter, you can't go away
for two months now.

13:02.721 --> 13:04.421
You'll miss Thanksgiving.

13:04.456 --> 13:06.056
I'm sorry, but you're
gonna have to choose

13:06.091 --> 13:07.758
between music and family.

13:07.792 --> 13:08.959
If I choose family,

13:08.994 --> 13:10.561
does it have to
be this family?

13:10.595 --> 13:12.296
Yes, Peter, this family.

13:12.330 --> 13:13.364
So make your choice.

13:13.398 --> 13:15.332
Very well,
this scavenger hunt

13:15.367 --> 13:17.801
will provide you
with my answer.

13:20.438 --> 13:22.740
Here it is--
a penny from 1858!

13:22.774 --> 13:24.808
We're getting closer
to our answer.

13:24.843 --> 13:27.945
Wake up, Mom!
He chose the music!

13:32.354 --> 13:33.854
(sighs)
You know, Quagmire,

13:33.888 --> 13:35.656
I feel kind of bad
leaving the family like this

13:35.690 --> 13:37.224
with Thanksgiving coming up.

13:37.259 --> 13:40.427
I mean, if I'm not there,
who's gonna carve the turkey?

13:40.462 --> 13:43.497
I don't understand!

13:43.531 --> 13:45.633
♪ On a tour
of one-night stands ♪

13:45.667 --> 13:48.302
♪ My suitcase and guitar
in hand ♪

13:48.336 --> 13:49.536
♪ And every stop

13:49.571 --> 13:51.605
♪ Is neatly planned
for a poet ♪

13:51.640 --> 13:55.476
♪ And a one-man band.

13:57.579 --> 14:02.049
♪ Everyone from Florida
is stupid ♪

14:02.083 --> 14:05.252
♪ Everyone from
Florida is dumb ♪

14:05.287 --> 14:07.288
♪ I might not be
the brightest guy ♪

14:07.322 --> 14:09.156
♪ But next to them,
my IQ's high ♪

14:09.190 --> 14:11.859
♪ If they had guitars,
here's how they'd strum ♪

14:13.928 --> 14:16.864
♪ Why the hell do you brush
your teeth at work? ♪

14:18.366 --> 14:21.769
♪ Why the hell do you brush
your teeth at work? ♪

14:21.803 --> 14:23.971
♪ The bathroom's
full of poop and pee ♪

14:24.005 --> 14:26.173
♪ And now you've rubbed
that on your teeth ♪

14:26.207 --> 14:29.510
♪ Like you're gonna kiss
someone at 3:00. ♪

14:31.379 --> 14:33.714
♪ Get out of the left lane

14:33.748 --> 14:37.351
♪ You stupid Asian bitch

14:37.385 --> 14:41.255
♪ I don't even know
why you are there. ♪

14:43.725 --> 14:48.128
♪ I...

14:48.163 --> 14:49.930
♪ Have become

14:49.964 --> 14:51.765
♪ Comfortably numb.

14:54.536 --> 14:55.502
Okay, Mr. Griffin.

14:55.537 --> 14:56.737
Now you've got
your flu shot.

14:56.771 --> 14:58.405
Will you stop
giving him flu shots, man?

14:58.440 --> 14:59.740
We got a show to do!

14:59.774 --> 15:02.376
Ah, Quagmire, it's cool,
it's cool.

15:02.410 --> 15:05.713
This is the doctor
that killed Michael Jackson.

15:08.583 --> 15:10.150
Yesterday, I learned
the difference

15:10.185 --> 15:11.752
between a train and a boat.

15:11.786 --> 15:13.454
I wrote this song
before that.

15:13.488 --> 15:15.456
♪ Train on the water

15:15.490 --> 15:17.257
♪ Boat on a track

15:17.292 --> 15:19.126
♪ Train on the water

15:19.160 --> 15:20.761
♪ Boat on a track

15:20.795 --> 15:24.131
♪ My lady took a train
across the Atlantic ♪

15:24.165 --> 15:28.235
<i>♪ I hope it don't sink
like the Titanic ♪</i>

15:28.269 --> 15:31.472
♪ I went to the station,
caught a boat downtown ♪

15:31.506 --> 15:35.309
♪ I hope it don't fall
off the track and I drown ♪

15:35.343 --> 15:36.343
Ladies and gentlemen,

15:36.378 --> 15:39.446
the All-Five-Foot-One
Black Albino Choir!

15:39.481 --> 15:41.148
♪ Train on the water

15:41.182 --> 15:43.016
♪ Boat on a track

15:43.051 --> 15:44.852
♪ Train on the water

15:44.886 --> 15:46.887
♪ Boat on a track.

15:48.656 --> 15:50.591
(guitars strumming)

15:50.625 --> 15:54.595
♪ This waitress is prettier
than my wife ♪

15:54.629 --> 15:58.699
♪ I could kill my family
with a knife ♪

15:58.733 --> 16:00.901
♪ We'll sail around
the world by ship ♪

16:00.935 --> 16:02.970
♪ I'll give my whole wad
as a tip ♪

16:03.004 --> 16:06.840
♪ But first I'll kill
my family with a knife ♪

16:06.875 --> 16:10.844
♪ Yes, he's gonna kill
his family with a knife ♪

16:10.879 --> 16:13.947
♪ Irregardless of this waitress,
I will kill them with a knife. ♪

16:13.982 --> 16:15.282
Hold it, hold it.
Stop the tape!

16:15.316 --> 16:17.384
You gonna fart in this
airtight booth all night?

16:17.419 --> 16:18.385
It wasn't me.

16:18.420 --> 16:20.053
We're the only
two people in here!

16:20.088 --> 16:21.955
Hey, Bobby, can you play
back Peter's track?

16:21.990 --> 16:23.590
PETER:
♪ This waitress

16:23.625 --> 16:26.627
♪ Is prettier than my wife...
(loud farting over track)

16:29.664 --> 16:32.099
Ah! Thank God.

16:32.133 --> 16:33.867
Come on, guys, you've
been bickering all ni...

16:33.902 --> 16:35.669
Oh, God!

16:35.703 --> 16:37.671
(muffled): We got the album
covers that Peter approved.

16:37.705 --> 16:38.705
Wait, wait, Peter,

16:38.740 --> 16:40.808
you approved these
without consulting me?

16:40.842 --> 16:42.609
Don't worry, they're great.

16:55.356 --> 16:57.024
I can be giggity.

16:57.058 --> 16:58.992
I can be goo.

16:59.027 --> 17:01.094
I can be giggity.

17:01.129 --> 17:02.663
I can be goo.

17:02.697 --> 17:05.299
Hey, Quagmire, wake up.
I got us twins.

17:05.333 --> 17:06.400
Peter, those are guys.

17:06.434 --> 17:08.602
Hell, yeah,
the Winklevoss twins.

17:08.636 --> 17:11.271
(whispering): They have
good ideas we can steal.

17:11.306 --> 17:12.506
Peter, quit
screwing around!

17:12.540 --> 17:14.541
We're about to go on
national television.

17:14.576 --> 17:17.244
Now, please welcome
our very special musical guests,

17:17.278 --> 17:19.279
Griffin and Quagmire.

17:22.917 --> 17:24.785
Wait, Quagmire, you got
something on your face.

17:24.819 --> 17:26.987
Aah! Damn it, Peter,
that was my eyebrow!

17:27.021 --> 17:28.155
Let's not make a scene.

17:28.189 --> 17:30.891
We're on TV.

17:30.925 --> 17:35.062
♪ You never should look
at your mother's boobies ♪

17:35.096 --> 17:39.099
♪ No matter how big
and round they are ♪

17:39.133 --> 17:43.604
♪ You'll end up seeing
something you don't wanna ♪

17:43.638 --> 17:47.574
♪ It's guaranteed to
leave a mental scar ♪

17:47.609 --> 17:51.678
♪ You never should look
at your daddy's penis ♪

17:51.713 --> 17:55.582
♪ When he's walking down
the hall on Sunday morn ♪

17:55.617 --> 18:00.220
♪ An acorn in a nest of twigs,
and underneath two fetal pigs ♪

18:00.255 --> 18:04.391
♪ It'll make you wish
you weren't even born ♪

18:04.425 --> 18:08.362
♪ Parents are gross,
parents are gross ♪

18:08.396 --> 18:12.165
♪ Parents are gross,
parents are gross... ♪

18:12.200 --> 18:14.001
Come on, you.
Get out of there.

18:14.035 --> 18:15.302
(music stops)

18:15.336 --> 18:17.037
(grunts)
My pick's in here.

18:20.542 --> 18:22.543
Come on!

18:27.715 --> 18:30.918
Come... Uhp, uhp, it just
skipped right over the strings!

18:30.952 --> 18:32.319
Yup, there it goes again.

18:32.353 --> 18:34.454
I saw it!
I totally saw it!

18:34.489 --> 18:37.224
All right, that's it!

18:37.258 --> 18:38.625
(crowd gasps)

18:38.660 --> 18:40.627
We're done!
Do you hear me? I quit!

18:42.630 --> 18:45.165
Hey, y-your makeup lady
was crying earlier.

18:45.199 --> 18:46.466
Wh-What was that about?

18:46.501 --> 18:48.402
This is my time.

18:48.436 --> 18:50.203
Don't ever (bleep)
talk to me

18:50.238 --> 18:52.439
during my time!

18:55.877 --> 18:58.812
Well, kids,
happy Thanksgiving.

18:58.846 --> 19:00.647
I wish Dad was here.

19:00.682 --> 19:02.249
Meg, could you zip up your fly?

19:02.283 --> 19:04.084
Th-That's kind of
wafting over here.

19:04.118 --> 19:05.919
(guitar strumming nearby)

19:05.954 --> 19:07.421
PETER:
♪ I can't poop

19:07.455 --> 19:09.089
♪ In strange places

19:09.123 --> 19:10.157
Peter?
Dad?

19:10.191 --> 19:11.191
Oh, boy.

19:11.225 --> 19:12.726
Larry, you got
to get out of here.

19:12.760 --> 19:14.061
It's been a great
two months!

19:14.095 --> 19:15.996
Meg, keep painting!

19:18.466 --> 19:23.203
♪ I'm so sorry
that I left my family ♪

19:23.237 --> 19:27.808
♪ And that I decided to roam.

19:27.842 --> 19:29.610
Peter, what are you doing here?

19:29.644 --> 19:31.845
Me and Quagmire kind
of had a falling out.

19:31.879 --> 19:33.680
And after that,
I-I realized I...

19:33.715 --> 19:34.815
Meg, can you please stop

19:34.849 --> 19:36.383
stuffing your face
for two seconds?

19:37.552 --> 19:39.319
Look, I'm sorry
for being a jerk,

19:39.354 --> 19:41.488
and letting a little fame
go to my head.

19:41.522 --> 19:43.824
I just hope you guys
can forgive me.

19:43.858 --> 19:46.326
Oh, Peter.

19:46.361 --> 19:48.161
(moans)

19:48.196 --> 19:49.963
I missed you so much.

19:49.998 --> 19:51.932
Oh, we missed you, too.

19:51.966 --> 19:53.333
But I understand.

19:53.368 --> 19:54.868
You had to go
chase your dream.

19:54.902 --> 19:56.770
And a part of me
is glad you did.

19:56.804 --> 20:00.140
But now I'm just happy
that you're home.

20:00.174 --> 20:01.341
Welcome home, Dad!

20:01.376 --> 20:03.977
So, did you get a lot of
trim on the road, Dad?

20:04.012 --> 20:06.013
Chris, that's inappropriate.

20:10.618 --> 20:13.020
QUAGMIRE:
Hey, you got room for another?

20:14.822 --> 20:15.922
Quagmire?

20:15.957 --> 20:17.758
I thought you were
still out on the road.

20:17.792 --> 20:19.493
I was, but then I thought,

20:19.527 --> 20:21.561
what was Simon
without Garfunkel?

20:21.596 --> 20:23.196
Wildly successful?

20:23.231 --> 20:25.098
Yeah, but all that success
would mean nothing

20:25.133 --> 20:26.733
if I lost my best friend.

20:26.768 --> 20:29.036
Do you... do you think
you can forgive me?

20:29.070 --> 20:31.104
Oh, Quagmire.

20:35.176 --> 20:37.878
Well, I'm glad to have you back
home for Thanksgiving, Peter.

20:37.912 --> 20:39.513
And I'm glad to be here.

20:39.547 --> 20:41.815
'Cause everyone knows
that life after being famous

20:41.849 --> 20:44.351
is even better
than it was before.

20:44.385 --> 20:45.816
Let me just grab my
stuff off the bus.

20:49.762 --> 20:51.130
(gunshot, thud)

20:51.131 --> 21:52.131
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru